Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from ISO/IEC
14496-2 (MPEG-4 Visual) and, for the short video header, ITU-T H.263, and
from published literature (IEEE Std 1180-1990 for the IDCT accuracy test).
They are not translations of, and do not derive from, any other MPEG-4
Part 2 or H.263 encoder's or decoder's source; none was read. The normative
tables (the variable length codes, the scans, the default quantiser
matrices, the escape-mode limits) are the standard's data, transcribed.

No other implementation was run, in development or in the tests. The
decoder is checked against other encoders' streams used as data only: the
sample bitstreams tools/fetch-samples.sh downloads from samples.ffmpeg.org
and fate-suite.ffmpeg.org (listed with their sources in docs/SAMPLES.md),
which are not redistributed with this crate.

